# The github.com/jack-work/msauth revision this repository's source requires.
#
# THIS IS THE COMPILE FLOOR: the OLDEST foundation revision this source can be
# built against. It moves when jacques starts depending on new foundation API,
# and not otherwise. 29679c9 is the revision that first carried msauth.LoadGate,
# which foundation_gate_test.go calls.
#
# It is deliberately NOT "the revision we last verified". That reading turns
# every client's suite red on every foundation commit until someone rebuilds,
# and a permanently red gate is one people learn to ignore. The fleet-wide
# "which artifacts does this commit oblige me to rebuild" question has its own
# instrument: msauth audit --fleet --required <rev>.
#
# jacques links the shared auth foundation as a Go LIBRARY, so a fix made in
# msauth reaches a user only when jacques is rebuilt and reinstalled. Nothing
# used to notice the gap: an installed jacques.exe could match jacques HEAD
# exactly and still carry auth code many foundation commits old.
#
# TestInstalledArtifactCarriesRequiredFoundation reads this floor and judges the
# installed binary against it. An artifact carrying this revision or any later
# one passes; anything older is a rebuild.
#
# The consequence worth stating plainly: a foundation SECURITY fix does not turn
# this gate red, because the compile floor did not move. The fleet sweep catches
# that; this gate is not the instrument for it.
29679c9
